# 000400-000499/20070523T132417Z_132924275.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=11ae|+Algorithm %3D%3D%0A%0AThe operation of diff is based on solving the [[Longest_common_subsequence_problem%7CLongest Common Subsequence]] (LCS) problem. In the LCS problem, you have two%0Asequences of items:%0A%0A        a b c d f g h j q z%0A%0A        a b c d e f g i j k r x y z%0A%0Aand you want to find the longest sequence of items that is present in%0Aboth original sequences in the same order.  That is, you want to find%0Aa new sequence which can be obtained from the first sequence by%0Adeleting some items, and from the secend sequence by deleting other%0Aitems.  You also want this sequence to be as long as possible.  In this case%0Ait is%0A%0A        a b c d f g j z%0AFrom the longest common subsequence it's only a small step to get%0Adiff%2Dlike output:%0A%0A        e   h i   k   q r x y %0A        %2B   %2D %2B   %2B   %2D %2B %2B %2B%0A%0A%3D%3D |=3b22|
